# Nested, inner & anonymous classes

## `static` nested — grouping & scoping

```java
public class HashMap<K, V> {
    static class Node<K, V> { ... }   // HashMap.Node — hidden helper
}
```

No link to an outer object. **Most nested classes should be `static`.**

## Inner (non-static) — bound to an instance

Reads the outer object's fields directly — but keeps it **alive** (leak risk). Use sparingly, on purpose.

## Anonymous — defined where used

```java
button.addListener(new ClickListener() {
    @Override public void onClick() { System.out.println("clicked"); }
});
```

One-off implementation, inline. Captures only **effectively final** variables.

## → lambdas

Single-method interface? Drop the ceremony:

```java
button.addListener(() -> System.out.println("clicked"));
```
